      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (messaging_store_name) (rate(corebankdemo_messaging_store_operations_total{outcome=\"added\", service_name=~\"$service\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "in {{messaging_store_name}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (messaging_store_name) (rate(corebankdemo_messaging_items_processed_total{outcome=\"completed\", service_name=~\"$service\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "out {{messaging_store_name}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Rows added versus rows completed, per store, whether a background processor or an inline path (instant-rail payments-outbox rows, corebank-inbox rows executed at intake) completed them. The dashed out-line meets the in-line once the backlog drains. Cancelled rows are not counted as out, so when faults cause cancellations, payments-outbox and corebank-inbox out stay below in by the number of cancelled payments."
